customer: young_entrepreneur
problem: email_virus
brief:
	As he sets the computer down, its CD tray goes out and in. He says the mouse moves by itself when he dials up with the modem; the player can't test that, he only tells it. Asked more, he admits an email with a "business opportunity" that he answered. The game doesn't push the emails, but this is the first hint to read them.

== drop-off
(neutral) Hello. New day, new obstacles to overcome on the path to success.
- Oh, I can see your computer is acting up again.
- That is not normal behavior.
(problem) Yeah. I mean, I can't concentrate when the CD tray is going in and out all the time. And every time I connect to the internet the mouse moves around by itself.
- That sounds really weird. Did you change anything lately?
(thinking) I didn't change a thing! Except maybe my future. I got this email with an excellent business opportunity so I'm now waiting to hear back from them.
- Sounds like you will have a brilliant future...
- Maybe an email virus then...
(neutral) Well, I trust you to take care of it!
(irritated01) And as I like to say: Time is money!
- I know, I know.

== pick-up
(irritated02) Now let's hope this was the last time I get interrupted on my mission for greatness.
- Fingers crossed.
- Just don't click on things you do not know what they are and you'll be fine.
(happy) Nice chatting with you but I have no time to waste! See you at the after work!
- ... when is it even?
